 "text": "Hey, good to hear from you. How are you? Usually down the middle or each contributing equally? That's a nice gesture from your parents. Your fiancé's parents not offering could make them feel like it's their wedding, not your shared celebration. Not rude, just a real difference in how wedding costs are seen. Many years ago, people usually got married at home by their parents. That's fair. Your fiancé is the one getting married, so it makes sense for them to lead on the finances. If his parents say no, you could ask if you could each contribute a different part of the wedding, like hotel rooms and shots, so your parents are covering the wedding and his parents none",
